# Garmr licensing

Garmr uses a **dual-licensing model**. Read this file together with
[`NOTICE`](NOTICE), [`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md),
[`TRADEMARKS.md`](TRADEMARKS.md) and [`COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md`](COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md).

## 1. Source code — AGPL-3.0-only

All original Garmr **source code** is licensed under the **GNU Affero General Public
License, version 3 only** (`AGPL-3.0-only`). The complete license text is in
[`LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt`](LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt).

    Garmr — self-hosted application-audit, insider-risk, and agentic
    security-monitoring platform.
    Copyright (C) 2026 Vetra Automation AB

    This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it
    under the terms of the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3, as
    published by the Free Software Foundation.

    This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT
    ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or
    FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU Affero General Public License
    for more details.

    You should have received a copy of the GNU Affero General Public License
    along with this program. If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.

Because Garmr is offered under AGPL-3.0-**only**, the "or (at your option) any
later version" clause does **not** apply.

## 2. Original documentation — CC-BY-4.0

Original Garmr **documentation** (the prose and diagrams authored by the Garmr
project, e.g. files under `docs/` and Markdown guides, unless a file's own header
says otherwise) is licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License** (`CC-BY-4.0`). The full text is in
[`LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt).

CC-BY-4.0 applies to documentation **only**. It does **not** apply to source code.
Code embedded in documentation (examples, snippets) is offered under the code
license (AGPL-3.0-only) so it can be copied into programs.

## 3. Trademarks — not licensed here

Neither the AGPL nor CC-BY grants any rights in the **Garmr** name, logo, or visual
identity. All such rights are reserved by Vetra Automation AB. See
[`TRADEMARKS.md`](TRADEMARKS.md).

## 4. Third-party components — their own licenses

Garmr includes third-party components (including vendored dependencies under
`vendor/`) that remain under **their own licenses**. Garmr as a combined work is
distributed under AGPL-3.0-only, but each third-party component keeps its original
license and copyright. See [`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md).
The Vetra Automation AB copyright does **not** extend to third-party files.

## 5. Commercial licensing — available separately

The AGPL's network-copyleft obligations do not suit every organization. Vetra
Automation AB, as the copyright holder of the original code, can offer the **same
code under separate commercial terms**. This is a possibility, not an automatic
grant: no commercial license exists until Vetra and the licensee execute a written
agreement. See [`COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md`](COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md).

## 6. Not legal advice

This file and the accompanying legal documents are informational and are **not
legal advice**. AGPL-3.0-only imposes real obligations (including source-availability
for users who interact with the software over a network). Organizations should obtain
their own legal review before deploying, modifying, or redistributing Garmr.

